// (3) Fill the K/V load pipeline STAGES-deep, then transpose each staged tile into sVt as
// its cp.async completes. The old code only kept ~1 load in flight (issue li+1, then block on
// loaded[li]); the fp8 dense config is long_scoreboard-bound (2.4 cyc/issue) because the
// consumer's full[] wait paces on the producer catching the loads. Priming STAGES tiles (so
// load[li] is already landed by the time the transpose reaches it) hides the load latency.
for (int li = 1; li < t.n_cnt && li < STAGES; ++li) issue_load(g + li, t.n_lo + li);
