1443	    // named barriers (8/9, cnt=256) staggers them by one step: while WG_a feeds the tensor core, WG_b runs
1444	    // softmax, and vice-versa. The token stays balanced across work items -- both WGs run the same n_cnt
1445	    // (same work index), so each does exactly one sync+arrive per inner-loop step. Gate: CM==128 (2
1446	    // consumer WGs) && HD==128. Big heads (192/256) are already tensor-pipe-saturated per tile so
1447	    // serializing the issue only adds barrier latency (-0.02 hd192/hd256). On the PERSIST path hd64
1448	    // measured a ~4% regression (1.25->1.20: its short HD=64 QK/PV leaves little softmax to overlap, so
1449	    // the extra barrier dominates) and hd96 was flat -- so unlike the per-tile kernel (HD<=128) the
1450	    // persist ping-pong is scoped to HD==128, where the win is real (local 0.89->0.96, causal 0.95->0.97,
